NEWS
====

This file summarizes user-visible changes to hostnamed, most recent first.
See the NEWS file for the full changelog.

0.3.0 (2026-10-14)
------------------
* Hostname-setting and machine-info changes from hostnamectl now use the
  system D-Bus API; the daemon performs persistence and polkit authorization.
* hostnamectl set-hostname no longer overwrites PRETTY_HOSTNAME unless
  the caller explicitly requests a pretty-hostname change.
* polkit is a required build dependency; the -Dpolkit option has been removed.
* Hostname validation follows strict RFC 1123 label rules for static and
  transient hostnames.
* GetProductUUID returns 16 raw UUID bytes and reports NotFound for missing,
  malformed, or placeholder UUIDs.
* Immutable hostname1 properties are marked EmitsChangedSignal=const in both
  the installed interface XML and embedded introspection data.
* Root polkit authorization is scoped to hostname1 actions; hostname
  operations use stable D-Bus errors and refresh property state on persistence
  error paths.
* Fixed duplicate/spurious Chassis and IconName PropertiesChanged entries.
* IconName follows the effective chassis; DefaultHostname and the default
  HostnameSource value are now populated.
* SetPrettyHostname preserves free-form dotted names instead of treating every
  dot as an FQDN separator.
* Interactive polkit challenges return
  org.freedesktop.DBus.Error.InteractiveAuthorizationRequired.
* Hardware model, vendor, serial, and chassis detection now have improved DMI
  fallback and device-tree support.

0.2.6 (2026-06-20)
------------------
* Polkit checks became asynchronous so authentication prompts do not block
  the daemon's main loop.
* GetProductUUID and GetHardwareSerial gained dedicated polkit actions.
* Fixed a polkit authorization bypass and a D-Bus JSON-escaping bug.
* Machine-info values are validated in the writer as defence in depth.

0.2.0 (2026-06-19)
------------------
* Added configurable os-release and machine-info paths.
* Improved pretty-hostname derivation from FQDN input.
* FirmwareDate is exposed as a D-Bus uint64 in microseconds since the Unix
  epoch.
* Machine-info property-cache updates emit PropertiesChanged directly.

0.1.0 (2026-05-31 - 2026-06-17)
--------------------------------
* First public implementation of org.freedesktop.hostname1 over plain D-Bus,
  without a systemd/logind dependency.
* Implemented hostname and machine-info setters gated by polkit.
* Added validation for hostnames and machine-info values.
* Added hostnamectl and localectl companion scripts and SlackBuild packaging.

BUGS
====

Known issues and limitations for version 0.3.0. These are not all release
blockers; some are design limitations or areas that still need testing.
Please report issues at https://github.com/nater1983/hostnamed/issues

* GetProductUUID and GetHardwareSerial default to the auth_admin polkit
  policy. This is stricter than systemd-hostnamed's upstream default and may
  surprise users porting polkit rules. Add local rules if unattended,
  non-interactive reads are required.
* The polkit authority handle is obtained at startup. If polkitd is not
  available then, the first later authorization may require a lazy re-fetch
  and introduce a one-time delay.
* write_machine_info_key() performs read-modify-write without advisory locking
  against another writer editing the file concurrently; concurrent updates
  can race.
* PrettyHostname derivation from an FQDN has not been exhaustively tested for
  IDN/punycode labels and unusual dotted input.
* CI builds the project and checks registered Meson tests and XML well-formedness,
  but there is not yet a comprehensive automated integration suite covering
  a live system bus, polkit agents, authorization denial, and filesystem failures.
* Changes made by external tools are detected through inotify. Very rapid
  successive writes may be coalesced, and behavior under heavy inotify queue
  load has not been stress-tested.
* Wheel-group membership changes are evaluated using the caller's session
  credentials; users may need to start a new login session for membership
  changes to take effect.
* Virtualization is not detected, so Chassis is not inferred as "vm" or
  "container"; the property is based on machine-info, SMBIOS, and device-tree
  data.
* The DMI placeholder list is finite; unknown firmware template strings may
  still be reported. Device-tree HardwareVendor is the lowercase compatible
  vendor prefix rather than a marketing name, and some boards do not provide
  chassis-type.
* Recovery after the system D-Bus daemon restarts has not been validated
  end-to-end; the daemon's name-loss/re-acquisition path may not recover
  reliably and should be tested under the target service supervisor.
* machine-info parsing supports double-quoted values and currently uses the
  first matching key if duplicate keys exist.
* Slackware startup behavior for fully qualified values in /etc/HOSTNAME should
  be verified against the target system's rc.S; hostnamed passes the configured
  static hostname to sethostname().
* Translation loading by the daemon has not been verified; bindtextdomain()
  may be needed for translations under po/.
